  "difficulty_reason": "Counted unit: the article's thm  (source0.tex lines 905-908). The statement reads: thm A space form ( c n, c) can be locally immersed into ( b N, b) , where N n , if and only if either c=b=0 or b/c + . Such local immersions can be extended to the whole manifold. Moreover, if N=n (when c=b=0 ), or if N = n+ b c n -1 (when b c + ), these immer. The retained complete proof (lines 909-983, 75 lines) is the article's own argument, retained line for line. It is a research-level argument in this field: it is not a routine verification but a complete proof whose steps (case analysis, intermediate estimates, comparison or induction arguments as the source words them) must all be carried out before the statement follows, which places it above ordinary PhD qualifying exercises, where such results are quoted rather than proved.",
